WEBVTT

00:00:03.149 --> 00:00:09.449
<v David Whitfield>Morning, everyone. Friday the twenty-fourth. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the Teams mime again?</v>

00:00:11.439 --> 00:00:17.390
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, got you. Only just made it in, mind. Traffic on the ring road was absolutely solid.</v>

00:00:19.489 --> 00:00:24.039
<v Callum Reid>Standard Friday, then. Everyone trying to start the weekend before they've started work.</v>

00:00:25.699 --> 00:00:30.250
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I was mostly trying to get past the same bus for twenty minutes.</v>

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:37.009
<v David Whitfield>Well, the heating in the portakabin thinks it's November. Lovely coming in here in July and getting slow-roasted.</v>

00:00:39.109 --> 00:00:42.960
<v Priya Raman>That explains the red face. Thought your camera had gone funny.</v>

00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:49.369
<v David Whitfield>No, that's genuinely me. Just having a moan, not adding the heating to the jobs.</v>

00:00:50.799 --> 00:00:54.649
<v Grace Liu>Good. We haven't got a column for lightly cooked mechanical engineer.</v>

00:00:56.229 --> 00:01:01.130
<v David Whitfield>Right, before we get onto the actions, anything already finished that needs taking off?</v>

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.409
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, finished the repair on the GT1 last night. That's done.</v>

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.140
<v David Whitfield>All closed, rather than something you're bringing into this morning?</v>

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.140
<v Tomasz Nowak>All closed. Just reporting it back, no new job there.</v>

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.650
<v Sarah Okafor>And I signed off the inspection on the GT2 Number 2 Bearing on Tuesday. That one's finished as well.</v>

00:01:26.299 --> 00:01:28.750
<v Priya Raman>Right, so that isn't a carry-over inspection?</v>

00:01:30.239 --> 00:01:33.390
<v Sarah Okafor>No, already signed off. It just keeps getting mentioned.</v>

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:41.859
<v Callum Reid>While we're on updates, I saw the pressure on the WHB dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.000
<v David Whitfield>Recovered without anyone doing anything?</v>

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.329
<v Callum Reid>Yeah. Just an observation, I'm not raising a job for it.</v>

00:01:50.879 --> 00:01:59.280
<v Grace Liu>Similar sort of thing here: saw the pressure on the GT2 bearing dip for a few minutes, then it came back on its own.</v>

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.540
<v Sarah Okafor>That's separate from the inspection I mentioned, just so we don't muddle those together.</v>

00:02:07.469 --> 00:02:11.319
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. Only passing on what I saw, not another inspection request.</v>

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.199
<v David Whitfield>Okay, actual actions now. Let's keep the closed stuff out of them.</v>

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:28.020
<v David Whitfield>I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the Line 1 Mould Temperature Controller on the 3rd. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:33.580
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, just the lock-out tag-out sign-off you're taking there, not a separate repair?</v>

00:02:35.439 --> 00:02:37.889
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, just that sign-off. I'll take it.</v>

00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:45.210
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Davey on that, on the 3rd. And keep the production hold against it so the priority's clear.</v>

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:49.330
<v David Whitfield>Exactly. Needs doing first, not disappearing halfway down the list.</v>

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:58.080
<v David Whitfield>Grace Liu, can you go to Kestrel to pick up the replacement parts for the pick and place on two?</v>

00:02:58.479 --> 00:03:01.629
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll do that. I can take the collection.</v>

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:07.539
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's collecting the parts, yeah? Not putting the fitting against the same action?</v>

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.960
<v David Whitfield>Correct, collection only. We're not adding a fitting job here.</v>

00:03:13.539 --> 00:03:19.840
<v Grace Liu>Fine. I'll go to Kestrel and pick up the replacement parts for the pick and place on two.</v>

00:03:20.919 --> 00:03:24.069
<v Callum Reid>We really do have some wonderfully short equipment names.</v>

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:30.740
<v Grace Liu>Still better than 'the thing beside the other thing', which is what I normally get.</v>

00:03:31.349 --> 00:03:37.300
<v David Whitfield>And Grace, can you do the pre-use checks on the forklifts by the 28th? That's fairly important.</v>

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.210
<v Grace Liu>Yep, accepted. By the 28th.</v>

00:03:42.699 --> 00:03:45.150
<v Priya Raman>Separate entry from the parts run, presumably?</v>

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:51.240
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, separate. The date and the fairly important bit are for the pre-use checks.</v>

00:03:53.449 --> 00:03:59.750
<v Grace Liu>Got it. I'll do the pre-use checks on the forklifts by the 28th. Two separate actions for me.</v>

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.740
<v David Whitfield>Right, the chiller next—</v>

00:04:04.949 --> 00:04:13.349
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, before you get into that, we can't get to the Line 3 Chiller until production gives us a window. That's still the blocker.</v>

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:19.899
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, after lunch is the intended slot, but we haven't got that access released yet.</v>

00:04:21.379 --> 00:04:27.329
<v David Whitfield>Olumide Adeyemi, can you recalibrate the sensors on the Line 3 Chiller after lunch? Top priority please.</v>

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:34.360
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Um, no, sorry, I can't take that one on. You'll need to give it to somebody else.</v>

00:04:35.779 --> 00:04:42.779
<v David Whitfield>Okay. Sarah, can you take that instead? Recalibrate the sensors on the Line 3 Chiller after lunch, top priority please.</v>

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:52.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, I'll take it instead. I'll recalibrate the sensors on the Line 3 Chiller after lunch, top priority, subject to getting that production window.</v>

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:59.610
<v Callum Reid>That's the distinction, yeah. Having an owner doesn't mean we've suddenly got access.</v>

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:05.910
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. After lunch stays the timing. I won't start before production releases it.</v>

00:05:07.939 --> 00:05:12.839
<v Priya Raman>So the blocker is the access, not a separate piece of work we're assigning?</v>

00:05:13.389 --> 00:05:16.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. I'm taking the recalibration, with that blocker still visible.</v>

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:24.310
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Oh, and before it gets mixed into this, the shutdown on the IM1 is cancelled now. Production need it running.</v>

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:28.170
<v David Whitfield>Right, cancelled. Not something we're carrying on today's action list.</v>

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.670
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Correct. No shutdown to do.</v>

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:38.639
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good to be clear. Hearing 'window' and 'shutdown' back-to-back makes it sound like the same conversation.</v>

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.480
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, different things. The IM1 shutdown is off.</v>

00:05:44.689 --> 00:05:52.740
<v Callum Reid>I'll chase the purchase order for the turbine one. Not an emergency but don't let it slip — that's how I'm treating it.</v>

00:05:53.779 --> 00:05:56.930
<v David Whitfield>Cheers, Cal. The purchase order chase is yours, then?</v>

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:03.829
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, mine. It doesn't need the emergency treatment, but I'm not letting it drift.</v>

00:06:05.899 --> 00:06:10.800
<v Priya Raman>And that's the order we're talking about, not an action on the equipment itself?</v>

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:15.490
<v Callum Reid>Just chasing the purchase order for the turbine one. Nothing else added.</v>

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:22.410
<v David Whitfield>Lovely. That's the actions agreed. Anything we've accidentally left sounding open that should be closed?</v>

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:27.589
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nothing from me. GT1 repair stays in the finished pile, please.</v>

00:06:29.319 --> 00:06:35.269
<v Grace Liu>And the pressure dip I mentioned stays as an observation. Not another job hiding in the notes.</v>

00:06:36.509 --> 00:06:41.060
<v David Whitfield>Yep, clear. Thanks, everyone. I'll stop baking in here and let you go.</v>
